  "$comment": "CONVERTER DATA ONLY (legacy/converter.md). This is not part of FoodBlock 1.6 and no node reads it. The converter uses it to turn a 0.x or 1.5 block into 1.6-shaped content before it applies the final steps in converter.md and re-signs. FoodBlock 1.6 (protocol.md, Encoding: Aliases): one table reads every earlier shape as 1.6. Read forever, never written; reading never changes a block or its hash. It applies to every block, with or without state.seq, in the order protocol.json `aliases.order` gives: `types` first (each old type name and the 1.6 type and kind it reads as; `fields` renames old state fields first; any other key, such as `status` or `channel`, is state the block read as when it said nothing; `retired` names a type that is no longer protocol, `outside` says where it went; a name with no row reads by `types_dotted`), then `shapes` (for the block's type.kind, then its type, then `*`, the rows for every type, as read so far; read again when a rule changes its type or kind), then `refs` (old ref names that mean the same on every type), then `outside` (a ref value with this prefix names someone with no record: an open side). A shape rule: `when` (paths that must hold: a value, \"*\" for present, null for absent, tested on the block as read so far); then, in this order, `refs` ({old ref: new ref}, renames on this type), `move` ({from path: to path}), `copy` ({to path: from path}), `join` ({to path: [paths]}, joined with '.'), `drop` ([paths]), `set` ({path: value}); then `type` and `kind` (a new reading); `settles` (the ref naming the block this one settles: a reader's mark, never written). refs, move, copy and set never write over a value the block already has there unless `force` is true. `envelope.ignored`: fields of an older envelope a reader ignores. `messages` renames message fields (asker and pusher read as signer). The grant rule `move` of state.last_good and state.last_counted to state.counted_to reads the merged field.",
